<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Entitlements for tools/a32/step0_xmem.c, signed ad-hoc in the arm32-harness step0 job.

    The harness asks the layer (husk-tl-xmem.c) for the two views of its JIT region. MAP_JIT --
    a writable-and-executable mapping -- is refused unless the process is signed with the JIT
    entitlement, so without this the runner can only ever exercise the layer's fallback view order.
    With it the runner grants the Fix A guest-facing view and the positive check
    (tl_xmem_guest_view_is_jit + "the guest's own arena executes") runs for real.

    These are the same bits the app carries (docs/02-jit-substrate.md): allow-jit is the macOS
    hardened-runtime entitlement for MAP_JIT; dynamic-codesigning is the plain key TrollStore
    honours on iOS. Signing is ad-hoc (no team), so nothing here is trusted by anyone -- it only
    asks this kernel for the mapping the harness is built to test.
  -->
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key><true/>
  <key>dynamic-codesigning</key><true/>
</dict>
</plist>
